  "prompt": "A one-time lookup is performed on an unsorted array of n values. Option A scans in O(n). Option B sorts a copy in O(n log n) and then binary-searches in O(log n). Ignoring constants, which strategy has the better complete asymptotic cost for this single query?",
  "options": [
    {
      "optionId": "scan",
      "text": "The scan, because O(n) is less than O(n log n + log n)."
    },
    {
      "optionId": "sort_binary",
      "text": "Sort plus binary search, because the final query is O(log n)."
    },
    {
      "optionId": "equal",
      "text": "They are asymptotically equal."
    },
    {
      "optionId": "binary_without_sort",
      "text": "Binary-search the unsorted array directly."
    }
  ],
